{
  "title": "Nam A2",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Two rows, two pages",
      "lines": [
        "32 blocks: 2 rows x 16",
        "columns. The screen and the",
        "pads show EIGHT of those",
        "columns at a time.",
        "",
        "The two ARROWS under the jog",
        "move that window. The footer",
        "says P1 or P2 when there is",
        "anything on the other page.",
        "",
        "A pad always means the column",
        "you can see: on P2 the first",
        "pad is column 9.",
        "",
        "Up/Down are NOT used - those",
        "are Move's octave buttons and",
        "taking one of a pair leaves",
        "you shifted with no way back.",
        "BOTH pad rows are blocks.",
        "  BOTTOM row = the main chain",
        "  TOP row    = a parallel row",
        "16 slots, not 8.",
        "TAP a pad to stomp it.",
        "HOLD a pad to edit it.",
        "JOG TURN sets where the two",
        "lanes meet again.",
        "JOG CLICK opens the menu.",
        "A NEW block arrives BYPASSED,",
        "so nothing jumps in your ears",
        "- tap the pad to bring it in."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Your own files",
      "lines": [
        "EVERY FOLDER IS NAMED AFTER",
        "THE LIST IT FEEDS. Drop a file",
        "in and it shows up there.",
        "  amps/     .nam -> Amp",
        "  od/       .nam -> OD",
        "  dist/     .nam -> Dist",
        "  fuzz/     .nam -> Fuzz",
        "  boost/    .nam -> Boost",
        "  cabs/     .wav -> Cab",
        "  reverbs/  .wav -> Reverb",
        "Yours appear AFTER the built-in",
        "pedals in each list, on knob 2.",
        "Upload them in the web manager",
        "(move.local:7700): Modules ->",
        "this one -> the folder's Manage",
        "button.",
        "Old installs: models/ and irs/",
        "are renamed for you on first",
        "run - nothing to move.",
        "",
        "NO RELOAD NEEDED. Upload a",
        "file and it shows up in the",
        "picker within a couple of",
        "seconds, while you are",
        "playing. The scan runs off",
        "the audio thread, so it does",
        "not touch the sound.",
        "A block keeps the capture it",
        "had, by NAME - the lists are",
        "sorted, so a new file landing",
        "ahead of yours would",
        "otherwise shift it onto its",
        "neighbour.",
        "Overwriting a file under the",
        "SAME name is the one case it",
        "cannot see; rename it or",
        "leave and re-enter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reading the board",
      "lines": [
        "It is a WIRE with boxes on it,",
        "like an Axe-Fx grid.",
        "  plain wire   slot is empty",
        "  closed box   in circuit",
        "  no side walls, wire through",
        "               = BYPASSED",
        "  FILLED box   the one you",
        "               are editing",
        "So a silent block is one you",
        "can see the signal going past."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The encoders",
      "lines": [
        "1  Block: Off, then",
        "   Amp Cab OD Dist Fuzz Boost",
        "   Dyn Filter Mod Delay",
        "   Reverb Pitch",
        "2  which pedal, capture, cab",
        "   or IR - one list each",
        "3-7  that block's own controls",
        "8  board output level",
        "Each category has its own pad",
        "colour; dim = bypassed.",
        "Input is on the menu."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Split and merge",
      "lines": [
        "SPLIT: put a block in the TOP",
        "row. It parts at that column.",
        "  top row    = LEFT",
        "  bottom row = RIGHT",
        "MERGE: turn the JOG. It walks",
        "the meeting point along the",
        "board. Out = they meet at the",
        "output (the default).",
        "The footer shows M:<col> the",
        "whole time the board is",
        "forked.",
        "A block outside the parallel",
        "part is drawn TALL: it feeds,",
        "or is fed by, both rails.",
        "Top-row pads PAST the merge",
        "are dark and do nothing -",
        "there is no signal there.",
        "Menu: Pan Top / Pan Btm."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tone Stack",
      "lines": [
        "At the END of the Amp list.",
        "The amp's own Bass/Mid/Treble,",
        "which a CAPTURE cannot have -",
        "a .nam is one setting of one",
        "amp and those knobs were",
        "already turned when it was",
        "taken.",
        "Amp  Fender/Marshall/Vox/Mdrn",
        "     - the scoop sits in a",
        "     different place on each",
        "Presence is the power amp, so",
        "it only boosts.",
        "It is the real passive circuit,",
        "not an EQ: Mid at 0 is a NOTCH",
        "(-10dB), and raising Bass FILLS",
        "that notch, as the pots do.",
        "PUT IT BETWEEN THE AMP AND THE",
        "CAB - that is where the circuit",
        "has it relative to the speaker.",
        "What it cannot do: change how",
        "the amp DISTORTS. That is baked",
        "into the capture."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Power Amp",
      "lines": [
        "Beside the Tone Stack, at the",
        "end of the Amp list.",
        "A .nam is a STATIC function -",
        "sample in, sample out, no",
        "memory. So every amp behaviour",
        "that depends on TIME is absent",
        "from it by construction, not",
        "missed by it. These are those.",
        "Sag   the supply drops as the",
        "      output draws current, so",
        "      a hard chord ducks and",
        "      swells back. Level",
        "      dependent - quiet",
        "      playing is untouched.",
        "Bloom how long it takes to come",
        "      back, 50-600ms",
        "Bias  the grid conducts on a big",
        "      transient and the valve",
        "      cuts off for an instant:",
        "      the spit on a hard pick,",
        "      the flub on a low note.",
        "Put it AFTER the capture."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tuning",
      "lines": [
        "Pitch > Tuning. Put it in b1,",
        "BEFORE the drive and the amp,",
        "or the amp answers the pitch",
        "you played and not the one",
        "you hear.",
        "1 Tune  named from the LOW",
        "        string. E is no",
        "        shift; Eb is one",
        "        semitone down, D is",
        "        two, C# three, C",
        "        four. F and F# go up.",
        "2 Fine  cents, -50..+50, to",
        "        match a record that",
        "        is not at concert.",
        "3 Mix   100 = the new tuning",
        "        alone. Lower it and",
        "        you hear BOTH, which",
        "        is a detune, not a",
        "        tuning.",
        "It costs 12ms of latency and",
        "that is inherent, not a bug:",
        "a read pointer running at a",
        "different rate has to start",
        "behind the write pointer.",
        "12ms is standing 4m from a",
        "cabinet.",
        "Big shifts warble. One or two",
        "semitones is what this is",
        "for; at four it is an effect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mic placement (Cab)",
      "lines": [
        "An IR is ONE mic in ONE place.",
        "These add the DIFFERENCE from",
        "there, which is what moving a",
        "real mic does.",
        "3 Pos   dust cap -> cone edge.",
        "        Loses the top, gains a",
        "        little body.",
        "4 Dist  SIGNED cm from where",
        "        the IR was captured.",
        "        - = closer: bass rise",
        "        + = further: air loss,",
        "            and REAL time of",
        "            flight (1ms/34cm)",
        "5 Mic   Off / 57 / 421 /",
        "        Ribbon / Cond - a",
        "        character on top",
        "6 Phase Norm / Inv",
        "Two cabs in the two lanes with",
        "different Dist comb exactly as",
        "two mics in a room do. That is",
        "7 Damp  WHICH POWER STAGE is",
        "        driving the cab. A",
        "        speaker is not a flat",
        "        load: its impedance",
        "        peaks at the cabinet",
        "        resonance (~95Hz) and",
        "        climbs above 1k. A",
        "        valve amp has poor",
        "        damping so it bumps at",
        "        both; an IR cannot",
        "        carry that - it was",
        "        measured through ONE",
        "        amp. 0 is tight, up is",
        "        a valve amp letting the",
        "        cabinet ring.",
        "Two cabs in the two lanes with",
        "different Dist comb exactly as",
        "two mics in a room do. That is",
        "what Dist is really for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reverb IRs and CPU",
      "lines": [
        "A cab IR is 23ms; a room is",
        "seconds. So LEN is a knob, and",
        "it is a CPU knob with a time",
        "written on it:",
        "   46ms  ~190us",
        "   93ms  ~380us",
        "  186ms  ~760us",
        "  372ms ~1520us of 2370",
        "Mix 0 is transparent - the dry",
        "is never touched, Mix only",
        "raises the wet.",
        "Pre   gap before the room",
        "      answers, 0-104ms",
        "LoCut keeps the tail out of the",
        "      low end, 20-400Hz"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reading the panel",
      "lines": [
        "Top right: CPU. Beside it, the",
        "OUTPUT METER - the tick is full",
        "scale, with room past it.",
        "Past the tick it INVERTS: the",
        "board is clipping, turn knob 8",
        "(Out) down.",
        "Under each knob is a bar. A +/-",
        "control fills from the CENTRE,",
        "so an EQ reads as a shape."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Real knobs",
      "lines": [
        "The pedals carry the controls",
        "the real ones have, with real",
        "units: 480ms, -6.0dB, 1.2k.",
        "Modulation rate is a PERIOD in",
        "ms, so you can match a tempo.",
        "Delays do ms or Note - set Mode",
        "and the Time knob becomes a",
        "division at the host's tempo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The two stereo ones",
      "lines": [
        "Doubler and Dimension write a",
        "side channel, so put them LAST -",
        "blocks after them see the centre",
        "only.",
        "Doubler: Width 0 = mono.",
        "Dimension has no rate knob on",
        "purpose - modes 1-3 widen with",
        "no audible cycle."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CPU is the limit",
      "lines": [
        "A frame has ~2370us of room.",
        "NAM Full ~1200us, Slim ~250us.",
        "Cab ~60us. A pedal 5-11us.",
        "So: one amp, and seven pedals."
      ]
    }
  ]
}